# WhatsApp AI Sales Agent - Codebase Review & Analysis

I have completed a thorough review of the **WhatsApp AI Sales Agent** codebase. Below is a detailed breakdown of the application architecture, database schemas, key files, and core mechanisms.

---

## 🏗️ System Architecture

The application is structured into two main parts:
1. **WhatsApp Automation Client & AI Agent**: Operates asynchronously to receive customer messages via WhatsApp, process them using LLM providers (with fallback layers and function tools), update the Prisma database, and reply.
2. **Admin Dashboard**: An Express-based server that serves a static frontend UI and REST endpoints to manage products, view orders/messages, adjust customer contact types, and access AI-driven business insights.

```mermaid
graph TD
    %% WhatsApp Flow
    WA[WhatsApp User] <-->|Baileys WebSockets| Client["WhatsApp Client (src/whatsapp/client.js)"]
    Client -->|Events| Handler["Message Handler (src/whatsapp/messageHandler.js)"]
    Handler -->|Filter & Log| Agent["AI Agent (src/ai/agent.js)"]
    Agent -->|Fallback Ordering| Fallback["Fallback Router (src/ai/fallback.js)"]
    Agent <-->|API Calls| Providers["AI Providers (Gemini, Groq, Qwen)"]
    Providers <-->|Function Calling| Tools["Database Tools (src/ai/tools/index.js)"]
    Tools <-->|ORM| DB[(SQLite Database)]
    Agent -->|Response| Sender["Message Sender (src/whatsapp/sender.js)"]
    Sender -->|Baileys Socket| WA
    
    %% Dashboard Flow
    Admin[Admin Owner] <-->|Browser| Dash["Admin Dashboard (public/dashboard)"]
    Dash <-->|REST API| Server["Express App (src/index.js)"]
    Server -->|APIs| APIRoutes["API Routes (src/routes/api.js)"]
    Server -->|Insights| InsightRoutes["Insights Routes (src/routes/insights.js)"]
    APIRoutes <-->|ORM| DB
    InsightRoutes <-->|Analyze| Advisor["Business Advisor (src/ai/businessAdvisor.js)"]
    Advisor <-->|ORM| DB
    Advisor <-->|Q&A / Insights| Providers
```

---

## 🗄️ Database Schema (`prisma/schema.prisma`)

The database uses **SQLite** (defined in [schema.prisma](file:///c:/Users/Aziry%20Tech/Desktop/whatsapp-ai-sales-agent/prisma/schema.prisma)) and maps out four core models:

1. **`Product` (`products`)**: Holds inventory details.
   - `id` (Int, PK)
   - `name` (String, e.g. *"Jezi ya Barcelona"*)
   - `category` (String, e.g. *Jezi, Simu, Laptop, Smartwatch, Calculator, Accessories*)
   - `price` (Float)
   - `stock` (Int)
   - `colors` & `sizes` (String, comma-separated values, e.g. *"S,M,L,XL"*)
   - `description` & `imageUrl` (String?)
   - `isActive` (Boolean, default `true` - used for soft deletes)

2. **`Conversation` (`conversations`)**: Represents a conversation session mapped to a WhatsApp phone number.
   - `id` (Int, PK)
   - `customerPhone` (String, unique JID format)
   - `customerName` (String?)
   - `status` (String, default *"active"*)
   - `needsHuman` (Boolean, default `false` - flags that AI failed/fallback was triggered)
   - `contactType` (String, default *"customer"* - can be set to *"personal"* so the AI ignores it)

3. **`Message` (`messages`)**: Contains chat logs (AI memory).
   - `id` (Int, PK)
   - `conversationId` (Int, FK to `Conversation`)
   - `sender` (String, *"customer"* or *"ai"*)
   - `content` (String)

4. **`Order` (`orders`)**: Logged purchase records.
   - `id` (Int, PK)
   - `conversationId` (Int, FK to `Conversation`)
   - `customerName` & `customerPhone` (String)
   - `productId` (Int?, FK to `Product` - nullable to allow retaining details if a product is deleted)
   - `productName` (String - copied directly from product to preserve receipt history)
   - `quantity` (Int, default `1`)
   - `color` & `size` (String?)
   - `deliveryType` (String, *"delivery"* or *"pickup"*)
   - `address` (String?)
   - `unitPrice` (Float? - records the item price at the exact moment of checkout)
   - `status` (String, default *"pending"* - options: *pending, confirmed, delivered, cancelled*)

